WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.060
- I've realized, right, trying to do the

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:04.550
international show,
that the cultural divide

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.330
is so much greater than we think.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:08.500
The biggest difference, I realized,

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.860
between us and our
American cousins, right,

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:14.160
when I went to California
was the attitude to drinking.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.070
Completely different!

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.550
I heard sentences in California

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.910
that I've never heard before in my life.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.097
Sentences like this,

00:00:21.097 --> 00:00:22.440
"Oh my God.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.370
Oh my God!

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.253
Did you see Larry?

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:31.116
Larry had four glasses
of wine with dinner!

00:00:31.116 --> 00:00:34.160
(audience laughing)

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.930
I think Larry may be an alcoholic"

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:39.319
(audience laughing)

00:00:39.319 --> 00:00:40.910
Yes, I know!

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:43.460
Four glasses of wine
with dinner in America,

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.160
you're an alcoholic!

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:47.440
Four glasses of wine
with dinner in Britain,

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.138
you're the designated driver!

00:00:49.138 --> 00:00:51.810
(audience laughing)

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:55.620
Last weekend, okay, we went
to Amsterdam, all right?

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:58.290
So, we're in Amsterdam,
and me and my chums

00:00:58.290 --> 00:00:59.210
rupe some diggers, right?

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:01.470
We're down this kind of backstreet

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.130
and one of them diggers, naughty guy,

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:07.891
okay, diggers is smoking
some of the weedy puff.

00:01:07.891 --> 00:01:09.610
(audience laughing)

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:11.390
Yeah, I'm not really into
it, as you probably guessed

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:13.690
by the fact that I just
called it weedy puff out loud.

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:14.530
(audience laughing)

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:15.363
Weedy puff.

00:01:15.363 --> 00:01:16.196
Weed.

00:01:16.196 --> 00:01:17.029
That's how normal people talk, Jack.

00:01:17.029 --> 00:01:18.780
No, so, he was smoking some weed.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:20.317
And he turns to me and he went, ya know,

00:01:20.317 --> 00:01:22.230
"Jack, do you wanna have a suck on this?"

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:23.730
Ah, not, not suck.

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:24.563
Not suck!

00:01:24.563 --> 00:01:26.870
That is not the word that he used.

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:27.845
That is not what he

00:01:27.845 --> 00:01:29.400
(laughing)

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.330
this story is going really well.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:32.010
Yeah, I was down a backstreet
with one of my friends

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:33.203
and he asked me if I
wanna have a suck on this.

00:01:33.203 --> 00:01:34.256
That is not

00:01:34.256 --> 00:01:36.410
(audience laughing)

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:37.330
I'm having a brain burp.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:38.163
Well, not suck.

00:01:38.163 --> 00:01:39.250
What's the word?

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:40.083
Puff!

00:01:40.083 --> 00:01:41.282
Thank you to the crack
whore down the front.

00:01:41.282 --> 00:01:43.527
(audience laughing)

00:01:43.527 --> 00:01:45.010
"Do you wanna have a puff on this weed?"

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:47.760
Anyway, I said no because, you know,

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:48.760
we're in public.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:49.593
It's not a great look.

00:01:49.593 --> 00:01:50.900
What if someone sees?

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:52.330
He went, "Jack, two things.

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:54.130
Firstly, it's legal.

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:55.970
Secondly, we're in Holland.

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:57.661
No one knows who the fuck you are.

00:01:57.661 --> 00:01:58.790
(audience laughing)

00:01:58.790 --> 00:01:59.880
Smoke it."

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:01.320
Now, I'm not proud, okay?

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.140
I gave in to the peer pressure.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:05.370
This is why you cannot smoke a spliff

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:08.460
on the street in the year 2017.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.260
I shit you not, as I put this spliff

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:14.130
to my lips, I looked up and the bloody

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:16.793
Google Maps car with the
360 camera was driving.

00:02:16.793 --> 00:02:19.155
(audience roaring)

00:02:19.155 --> 00:02:21.127
(audience clapping)

00:02:21.127 --> 00:02:24.127
(audience cheering)

00:02:31.779 --> 00:02:33.630
There's certain situations in life, right,

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.430
where every time I fall apart.

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:36.930
Complaining is one of them.

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:38.950
Passport control, that's another.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:40.150
Can't do it.

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:41.850
And I don't have anything to hide.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:45.359
(laughing)

00:02:45.359 --> 00:02:47.470
I mean, it doesn't help that I have

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:51.510
the creepiest passport photo
that has ever been taken.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:52.790
People looking at me thinking you've got

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:56.690
a bad passport photo, you
have not seen anything yet.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:59.323
Brace yourselves for this shit.

00:03:00.597 --> 00:03:01.632
(audience laughing)

00:03:01.632 --> 00:03:03.206
[Jack] What is that?

00:03:03.206 --> 00:03:05.313
(laughing)

00:03:05.313 --> 00:03:08.249
I look like I've just taken
Liam Neeson's daughter.

00:03:08.249 --> 00:03:10.920
(audience laughing)

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.487
Yes, very funny,
Benedict, we can all read.

00:03:13.487 --> 00:03:16.200
(audience laughing)

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.340
So, every time I approach passport control

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:19.700
that is in my head.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:21.300
That I'm about to hand that over.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:24.390
It does not excuse how much I fall apart

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:27.410
under the most basic of questioning.

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:28.327
I walk up, I'm like,

00:03:28.327 --> 00:03:29.160
"Hello."

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.817
"Where are you traveling from today, sir?"

00:03:30.817 --> 00:03:32.030
"France. No, Spain.

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:33.330
Shit, sorry, Italy.

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:34.163
Don't know why I said that.

00:03:34.163 --> 00:03:35.130
Didn't sleep on the plane.

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:36.060
Drugs didn't work.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:37.500
Not drugs, like, drugs, drugs.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.950
I mean, drugs like sleeping pill drugs.

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:39.840
I don't have any drugs on me.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:40.673
I promise you I'm not a mule.

00:03:40.673 --> 00:03:42.030
Don't look at my bottom.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.209
I have explosive diarrhea.

00:03:43.209 --> 00:03:44.350
Not explosive like a bomb.

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:45.183
Shit!

00:03:45.183 --> 00:03:46.016
Just said bomb in an airport.

00:03:46.016 --> 00:03:46.849
Well, it's just a word.

00:03:46.849 --> 00:03:48.140
The more you say it, the
less offensive it becomes.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:49.020
Bomb, bomb, bomb.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:49.853
Oh, it's like a song.

00:03:49.853 --> 00:03:50.960
Bomb, bomb, bomb, bomb, bomb.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.140
I'll stop saying bomb now cause you're

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.330
all looking at me like I'm a terrorist.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:54.790
I promise you I'm not a terrorist.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:55.623
I'm just Jack.

00:03:55.623 --> 00:03:56.456
Plain old Jack.

00:03:56.456 --> 00:03:57.289
Hi, Jack.

00:03:57.289 --> 00:03:58.146
Not highjack!

00:03:58.146 --> 00:03:58.979
Shit, no!

00:03:58.979 --> 00:03:59.812
Don't shoot!"

00:03:59.812 --> 00:04:02.812
(audience cheering)

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:06.390
Why do people think it's acceptable

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.580
to cut in line at airports?

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:11.540
Never acceptable to barge
the line, all right?

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.920
Some people think there are exceptions.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.253
Like, if you're late.

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:17.143
Not an excuse.

00:04:17.143 --> 00:04:18.070
(audience laughing)

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:20.500
I was waiting to check in in
the airport the other day,

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:22.980
this woman comes barging to the front

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:24.457
and proffers this bullshit.

00:04:24.457 --> 00:04:26.700
"Sorry, excuse me,
sorry, excuse me, sorry.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.427
I've got to get a flight."

00:04:28.427 --> 00:04:30.208
(audience laughing)

00:04:30.208 --> 00:04:32.093
Well, no shit Sherlock!

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:35.627
We're in a fucking airport!

00:04:35.627 --> 00:04:36.700
Why do you think I'm here?

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:38.281
To buy a bit Toblerone?

00:04:38.281 --> 00:04:39.626
Hm?

00:04:39.626 --> 00:04:41.880
Please let me get out of
your way with these bags

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.040
which I just take with me everywhere!

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:45.281
Back of the line!

00:04:45.281 --> 00:04:46.389
(audience laughing)

00:04:46.389 --> 00:04:47.670
The reason I hate traveling is cause

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:49.580
I can't sleep in public.

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:50.910
And I can't sleep in public because

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:52.873
I sleep with my eyes open.

00:04:52.873 --> 00:04:53.706
(audience laughing)

00:04:53.706 --> 00:04:55.420
Medical condition, not just a habit

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:56.856
from boarding school.

00:04:56.856 --> 00:04:58.359
(audience roaring)

00:04:58.359 --> 00:04:59.734
Watch it!

00:04:59.734 --> 00:05:01.672
(laughing)

00:05:01.672 --> 00:05:02.980
Apparently 4% of the population

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:03.820
sleep with their eyes open.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:05.220
Does anyone else?

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:06.520
No, no one.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:07.930
Well, there might be
some and we don't know.

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:09.013
They've nodded off.

00:05:09.013 --> 00:05:09.962
(laughing)

00:05:09.962 --> 00:05:12.962
(audience laughing)

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:17.090
Mine's not the whole
way, but if I fall asleep

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:18.010
with my contact lenses in,

00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:19.260
it's pretty peculiar.

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:21.000
A friend of mine took a
photograph of me recently

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.640
passed out in public.

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:24.520
This is the look we're going for.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:25.353
Yeah!

00:05:25.353 --> 00:05:26.186
(audience laughing)

00:05:26.186 --> 00:05:27.087
Hello ladies!

00:05:27.087 --> 00:05:29.100
(audience laughing)

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.173
Such an embarrassing photo of me

00:05:30.173 --> 00:05:31.650
to have to show you.

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:34.027
Please don't tell anyone
that I was on a bus.

00:05:34.027 --> 00:05:36.944
(audience roaring)

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:39.390
So bad, this situation.

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:42.990
So bad, right, that someone
complained about me once

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:44.780
on a plane.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:45.613
I know.

00:05:45.613 --> 00:05:48.557
I was like, "Uh, it is a
medical condition, okay?"

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:52.080
But looking back on it
now, I can kind of see it

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.390
from my fellow passenger's perspective.

00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:58.620
Because he did not know that
I slept with my eyes open.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:01.730
Also, not the only trick
that my body plays on me

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:02.693
when I fall asleep.

00:06:02.693 --> 00:06:03.640
(audience laughing)

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:05.614
Yeah, a couple of you
are ahead of me, yeah?

00:06:05.614 --> 00:06:06.530
(audience laughing)

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:08.340
I imagine from my fellow passenger

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:10.730
it was quite unnerving
that for the duration

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:12.340
of a three hour flight,

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:14.740
every time he turned to his left,

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.820
the passenger in the seat next to him

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:18.950
appeared to be slumped there,

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:21.300
gazing into his eyes,

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:24.180
drool tumbling from my bottom lip,

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:25.802
nursing a semi.

00:06:25.802 --> 00:06:28.842
(audience laughing)

00:06:28.842 --> 00:06:31.447
(audience clapping)

00:06:31.447 --> 00:06:34.447
(audience cheering)

